# Superpowers integration (Redux)

Superpowers is installed via Cursor Agent marketplace (`/plugin-add superpowers`). See [docs/SUPERPOWERS.md](../../docs/SUPERPOWERS.md).

## Role

Use Superpowers for **process**: clarify intent before coding, systematic debugging, verification before claiming success, and structured review — especially on non-trivial or ambiguous work.

## Precedence

1. Current Linear/issue scope and user instructions.
2. [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md), `/docs`, and Redux `.cursor/rules` (especially `engineering-quality.mdc` and domain rules).
3. CI commands in [docs/DEVELOPMENT.md](../../docs/DEVELOPMENT.md) — run them; do not claim pass without output.
4. Superpowers skills — follow when they **complement** the above; never override Redux stack conventions, tenancy/auth, or “smallest correct diff.”

## Do not duplicate

Do not restate Superpowers skill text in this repo. Do not add parallel “methodology” rules that repeat `engineering-quality.mdc`.

## Tests

This repo has **no** unit/e2e runner yet. Do not add throwaway tests to satisfy TDD rhetoric. If TDD is appropriate, treat “add test runner + first real tests” as its own scoped task aligned with `pnpm run test` / CI.

## Git / PRs

Superpowers may suggest merge/PR flows. **Manual Cursor:** no branch/commit/push/PR unless the user asks ([docs/MANUAL_DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW.md](../../docs/MANUAL_DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW.md)). **Cloud Agent / Linear:** follow [docs/CLOUD_AGENT_WORKFLOW.md](../../docs/CLOUD_AGENT_WORKFLOW.md); never auto-merge.
